# Demand barks for OracleCommunard, the NCWL's counterpart to the Oracle. The system upcases
# these before speaking them. Deliberately materialist - a quota handed down and a ration paid
# out - with none of the Oracle's gnosis, grace or divinity.

oracle-communard-demand-1 = The plan is amended. The commune requires one {$item}.
oracle-communard-demand-2 = One {$item} to the collective. Nothing is asked of you that is not asked of everyone.
oracle-communard-demand-3 = Quota for this shift is one {$item}. Meet it.
oracle-communard-demand-4 = Bring one {$item}. What you surrender to the League, the League returns in kind.
oracle-communard-demand-5 = The committee has voted. One {$item}, from whoever stands nearest.
oracle-communard-demand-6 = A worker who withholds one {$item} withholds it from the whole front.
oracle-communard-demand-7 = There is no grace here and none is offered. There is one {$item}, and there is the ration that follows it.
oracle-communard-demand-8 = One {$item}. The Union does not beg for what is already owed to it.
oracle-communard-demand-9 = The front does not wait on your hesitation. One {$item}!
oracle-communard-demand-10 = Requisition order, one {$item}. Log it with your shift committee or do not. It changes nothing.
oracle-communard-demand-11 = Kane did not ask Vaucelles politely. Bring one {$item}.
oracle-communard-demand-12 = One {$item} into the common stock. The oil already belongs to all of you.

oracle-communard-feedback = THE PLAN IS POSTED ON THE WALL. WHY ARE YOU READING ME INSTEAD OF IT?
